# Perimeter Platform — Women Safety Social Community Platform Implementation Plan

Transform Perimeter into a community-based women safety social platform (inspired by social networks like Instagram, centered around women's safety, incident reporting, verified emergency dispatch, and case follow-ups).

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Complete Removal of `login.html` & Pure One-Time Persistent Registration:**
> `frontend/login.html` will be permanently deleted. All links, redirects, server default fallbacks, and scripts referencing `login.html` will be updated to point to `register.html` or the authenticated dashboard.
> When opening `http://localhost:8080/`:
> 1. If an active JWT session exists in `localStorage`, the user is immediately routed to their designated role dashboard (`user.html`, `volunteer.html`, `police.html`, `journalist.html`, `admin.html`).
> 2. If no valid session exists, `register.html` is displayed. Registration saves the user to SQLite, issues a signed JWT, and immediately logs them in persistently.
> 3. For development & testing convenience, `register.html` will feature a quick-switch persona selector that authenticates pre-seeded test roles (`Aarohi Sharma`, `Inspector K. Patil`, `Priya Deshmukh`, `Rhea Nair`, `Admin`) in 1 click without retyping.

> [!NOTE]
> **Data & Feature Continuity:**
> All existing working features (Emergency SOS button, 5km Geofence spatial router, active dispatch cards, volunteer accept flow, police resolution, case timeline audit, admin stats) will be 100% preserved and cleanly integrated into the unified social architecture.

